    "result_text": "All 295 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `sharesHousehold` on the owner-creation response, following the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (a read-only, computed-at-creation, non-persisted attribute):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean sharesHousehold` field with getter/setter (matching the `namesakeCount` transient precedent). MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 before persisting, sets `sharesHousehold` via a new `sharesHousehold(address, city)` helper that scans existing owners for one already having the same address **and** city (matched case/whitespace-insensitively via the existing `normalize` helper, consistent with the other duplicate checks). It's computed against the owners present before the new owner is saved, so the owner never matches itself. Creation still proceeds regardless of the result.\n\nThe `Cp17Tests.coreHouseholdFlag` acceptance test passes (first owner \u2192 `false`, second at same address+city \u2192 `true`), and the full suite remains green.",
